# ============================================================================
#  .deploy.env.example — template. Copy to .deploy.env (gitignored) and fill
#  in the 3 values below.
#
#      cp .deploy.env.example .deploy.env
#
#  These drive a non-interactive (Cloudflare API) deploy via wrangler — no
#  browser `wrangler login`. Same pattern as simplenote-mcp. Never commit
#  .deploy.env.
# ============================================================================
#
#  HOW TO FILL EACH VALUE
#  ----------------------
#  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#    dash.cloudflare.com → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token →
#    "Create Custom Token". The Workers template is NOT enough — bookworm
#    also provisions R2 and D1. Grant exactly:
#        Account · Workers Scripts    · Edit
#        Account · Workers R2 Storage · Edit
#        Account · D1                 · Edit
#        Account · Account Settings   · Read     (lets wrangler verify auth)
#        User    · User Details       · Read
#    Account Resources: Include → your account.
#
#    Note: if R2 has never been enabled on the account, open
#    dash.cloudflare.com → R2 once and activate it (it may ask for billing
#    info; the 10 GB free tier still costs $0).
#
#  CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#    dash.cloudflare.com → Workers & Pages → "Account ID" in the right sidebar.
#
#  ADMIN_TOKEN
#    You choose this — the shared secret that guards the book-upload endpoint
#    (scripts/publish-book.mjs sends it as a Bearer token). Generate one:
#        openssl rand -hex 24
#
#  DEPLOY FLOW (scripts/deploy.sh does all of this)
#  ------------------------------------------------
#    1. Verify token      — `wrangler whoami`
#    2. D1 database       — create `bookworm`, patch id into wrangler.jsonc
#    3. R2 bucket         — create `bookworm-books`
#    4. Schema            — apply schema.sql to remote D1
#    5. Deploy            — `wrangler deploy`, yields the *.workers.dev URL
#    6. Secret            — push ADMIN_TOKEN
#    7. Live probe        — GET /api/books on the deployed URL
# ============================================================================

# --- Cloudflare API auth (drives wrangler without `wrangler login`) ---
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Worker secret (pushed via `wrangler secret put`) ---
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Web Push (新書通知), optional ---
#  VAPID_PRIVATE_JWK
#    The application-server keypair for Web Push, as a private JWK:
#        node scripts/gen-vapid.mjs
#    Single-quote it (JSON contains commas and quotes). deploy.sh pushes it
#    as a worker secret when set; CI reads it from the repo secret of the
#    same name. Leave empty to ship without notifications. Rotating it
#    invalidates every subscription — DELETE FROM push_subs after a swap.
#
#  VAPID_SUBJECT
#    Your contact address, sent to push services (Apple/Google/Mozilla) in
#    every notification's VAPID token so they can reach the operator of this
#    application server: `mailto:you@example.com` or an https URL. Required
#    if you enable push — the worker keeps push disabled until both values
#    are set, so an install always announces itself under its own contact.
VAPID_PRIVATE_JWK=
VAPID_SUBJECT=
